Chapter: LocationSensorsStub
  cites Foreword chapter LocationStub
  cites Foreword chapter SensorsStub

 The two stubbed effects, performed.

 What this pins is not the numbers, which are arbitrary and say so. It
 is that a program CAN perform them: before this, mentioning locate
 type-checked and then died at emit with CDX2040, so no program using
 location could be built at all. Every line below is an operation
 actually performed through its effect row.

 The two `fixed` lines are the load-bearing ones. Both must read False.
 If a future chapter drives real hardware and forgets to flip its own
 answer to True, a caller has no way to tell a reading from a placeholder,
 and this test is the thing that says so out loud.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Location, Sensors] Nothing = act
    lfx <- location-is-fixed
    fix <- locate
    alt <- altitude
    sfx <- sensors-are-fixed
    acc <- accelerometer
    gyr <- gyroscope
    bar <- barometer
    lux <- light-level
    print-line-uni ("location fixed " & show lfx)
    print-line-uni ("locate " & show (fix.lf-latitude) & " " & show (fix.lf-longitude))
    print-line-uni ("altitude " & show alt)
    print-line-uni ("sensors fixed " & show sfx)
    print-line-uni ("accel " & show (acc.sx-x) & " " & show (acc.sx-y) & " " & show (acc.sx-z))
    print-line-uni ("gyro " & show (gyr.sx-x) & " " & show (gyr.sx-y) & " " & show (gyr.sx-z))
    print-line-uni ("barometer " & show bar)
    print-line-uni ("light " & show lux)
  end
